  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "GROUNDING: The claim that 755 rows remain after filtering is not shown in the printed output; the number of -999 rows was not displayed, so this figure cannot be verified.",
    "GROUNDING: The statement that the treatment arm has \"more mild and severe patients\" contradicts the cross‑tab output (treatment has far fewer mild patients than control).",
    "OVERREACH: The answer labels the difference as a \"treatment effect\" despite only adjusting for severity; other confounders remain unaddressed, making a causal interpretation unwarranted.",
    "UNACKNOWLEDGED DATA PROBLEMS: The analysis notes 712 patients after deduplication but does not explain why this is far below the expected 800, nor does it discuss the impact of the large imbalance in severity distribution between arms on the weighted average method used."
